# ── GENERATED, and deliberately not kept (D-6) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below regenerates from Dan's two jars plus one network fetch in about ten seconds:
#
#     node tools/fetch-vanilla-data.mjs
#     node tools/suite.mjs
#
# A generated registry that has to be kept is a registry that can quietly drift from the game.
# Session 2 met the other failure mode as well: an input nothing fetched, downloaded by hand,
# lost with the container, and nowhere in any document. If a number in the docs cannot be
# reproduced by running the suite, the number is wrong.
#
# These are also Mojang's assets, extracted from Dan's own copies of the game, and they do not
# belong in a shareable repository under any circumstances.
assets/
mcdata/
dist/

# The built deliverable and the gallery. Both are outputs of `node build.mjs` and
# `node tools/build-gallery.mjs`; committing 7 MB of generated base64 on every change would
# make the history useless for reading.
mclite.html
gallery.html
screenshot.png

# transfer and scratch
_xfer.tar.gz
*.tar.gz
node_modules/

# session screenshots - big, and regenerated by the checks
Claude outputs/
*.bundle

# the vanilla data cache: generated by tools/fetch-vanilla-data.mjs, ~10 s, never kept (D-6)
.mcdata/
# the packed-sound cache: generated by tools/pack-sounds.mjs from Dan's own jar, never kept
.mcsnd/
# machine-specific paths, written once per machine, never shared
mclite.config.json
# Dan's own copies of the 1.18.2/1.13.2 jars, staged per-machine beside the project (tools/paths.mjs)
jars/

# ⚠ `rm` is blocked on the Cowork device mount, so git cannot unlink its own lock files and
# nothing here can delete a scratch file. Everything that would otherwise be removed is MOVED
# into .trash/ instead — stale .git/index.lock and HEAD.lock after a successful commit, and any
# working file an agent had to displace. Delete it from a shell that can unlink.
.trash/

# ⚠ RAW DISASSEMBLY IS MOJANG'S CODE, NOT A DERIVED NUMBER (D-6). `tools/golden/*.tsv` and
# `noise-golden-1.18.2.json` are VALUES read out of the game — a friction of 0.98, a colour, a
# noise sample — and they are committed because the project's whole discipline is that a constant
# must be traceable. `javap.*.txt` is the compiled method bodies themselves and stays local; it
# regenerates in about a minute from the jobs lane (`_mclite/*_dump.js`), which is where the
# procedure lives.
tools/golden/javap.*.txt

# session transfer archives (D-360: the cloud container and this machine swap one file)
*.tgz

# the project-local headless Chrome (D-407): `node tools/get-chromium.mjs` regenerates it, ~1 min
.chromium/

# the suite ledger (D-408): written by every run, read by session.mjs start; per machine, never shared
.ledger/

# desktop Code-tab worktrees (D-410): never versioned
.claude/worktrees/

# Syncthing (Dan added MCLITE to the cluster in session 55) — its marker folder is not ours
.stfolder/
.stversions/
*.sync-conflict-*

# the file-queue shell runner (D-438): inbox/done/logs are per-machine runtime, never shared
.shell/

.claude/started.json
.claude/breaches.log
.claude/loop.json
.claude/loop-log*.jsonl
.claude-auth/
_to_delete/

# readable 1.18.2 source, rebuilt per D-488 recipe (.claude/loop-prompt.md §2A), Mojang code, never committed
.decomp/
_xfer/

# the vanilla golden pregen (D-549): ~100 MB of Mojang-generated region files, rebuilt by
# `node tools/vg_pregen.mjs` on a machine with Java
/golden/

# infra task hand-off bundles (Dan, 23 Sept) — the loop merges them
.infra/

# s112: loop clones symlink these six dirs; the trailing-slash patterns above do not match a symlink
/assets
/jars
/.mcdata
/.mcsnd
/.chromium
/.decomp

# throwaway live-browser driver output (petmobpeek.mjs, ravagerchargepeek.mjs, etc.) — screenshots
# and JSON dumps kept on disk for re-run convenience only, regenerated every run, never committed
tools/out/
_status/

# hosted runners (Dan, 6 Oct): the data branch checkout and shard outputs
_store/
shard-out/
shard-all/

logs/
tools/mobproof/
